      "page_title": "The ERR Trap and set -e",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When ERR Fires"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`trap handler ERR` fires when a command returns ==non-zero==",
            "Same rules as `set -e` — one shared definition of failure",
            "NOT in `if`/`while` conditions, `&&`/`||` operands, `!`-negated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "set -Eeuo pipefail",
            "trap 'echo \"FAIL line $LINENO: $BASH_COMMAND (rc=$?)\" >&2' ERR"
          ],
          "note": "single quotes: expands when it fires"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pipelines Hide Failures"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Without `pipefail`, `false | true` succeeds",
            "Status is the LAST element's, so errors vanish mid-pipe",
            "`PIPESTATUS` holds every element's status",
            "Read it immediately — the next command clobbers it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Handlers, Two Jobs"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "cmd fails",
              "ERR: diagnose",
              "set -e abort",
              "EXIT: clean",
              "exit rc"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ERR runs first — report `$?`, `$LINENO`, `${BASH_SOURCE[0]}`",
            "Add `${FUNCNAME[@]}` for a usable stack trace",
            "EXIT runs after, for teardown only — do not mix them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Opting Out On Purpose",
          "items": [
            "`cmd || true` exempts one command from `set -e` and ERR",
            "Comment WHY, or someone re-breaks it later",
            "`cmd || die \"msg\"` beats `set -e` when each failure differs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A subshell is a forked copy of the whole shell",
            "Variables, traps and options are copied, not shared",
            "Nothing set inside can reach back to the parent"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
