  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of BASH TRAPS & SIGNALS. Your script creates a temp dir, then dies to Ctrl-C — and leaves the mess behind. This handbook is the full field guide to Bash traps: EXIT vs ERR vs INT, why double quotes in a trap string freeze the wrong value, how an empty `$tmpdir` turns `rm -rf $tmpdir/*` into `rm -rf /*`, and the two-phase TERM-then-KILL pattern for children that spawn children. Ten pages, from signal numbers to a production skeleton you can paste today.",
